$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of
5,5-Disubstituted Hydantoins Under Conventional Heating Conditions All of
5,5-disubstituted hydantions were synthesized by the method of
Bucherer-Bergs shown in Scheme 1. Following this procedure, 5 mmol of
aldehyde or ketone was dissolved in 7mL of 50% ethanol. The freshly
powdered ammonium carbonate (2.40 g) and 0.42 g of potassium cyanide (6.5
mmol) were dissolved in 7mL H2O. The mixture was placed in a
round-bottomed flask. The reactants were mixed and irradiated at
microwave oven for the period as indicated in Table 1. The progress of
the reaction was monitored by thin-layer chromatography (TLC, ethyl
acetate/petroleum ether = 1:1.3 v/v). After the completion, the reaction
mixture was chilled in an ice bath. The solution was neutralized with
diluted hydrochloric acid. The solvent was removed under reduced
pressure. The product was collected by filtration and washed with
EtOH/H2O (1:1). The product was dried and recrystallized from 95%
ethanol. The products were identified by comparing their physical and
spectral data with those of authentic samples.
5-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-imidazolidine-2,4-dione (C10H10N2O3, 2c)
5,5-diphenylhydantoin (C15H12N2O2, 2i) White needles. Mp: Rep. 295-296;
Lit. 297-298 g ; UV (CH3OH) λ max: 276 nm; 1H NMR (DMSO-d6 , 400 MHz) δ:
11.1 (s, 1H, N3-H), 9.33 (s, 1H, N1-H), 7.36 (m, 10H); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6 )
δ: 175.26 (C=O), 156.43 (C=O), 140.39 (2C), 128.96 (2CH), 128.48 (4CH),
127.04 (4CH), 70.66 (Cspiro); IR (KBr cm-1) ν: 3270 (N-H, s), 3200 (N-H,
s), 1770 (C=O, m), 1730 (C=O, s), 1710 (C4=Oasym, s), 1400 (N-H, b), 760
(=C-H, b), 740 (=C-H), Anal. Calcd. for C15H12N2O2 (252.249): C 71.42, H
4.79, N 11.10, O 12.68; Found: C 71.45, H 4.80, N 11.12, O 12.66; M.S.
(m/z): 252 (M+, 56), 223 (44), 209 (39), 180 (100), 165 (23), 104 (56),
77 (42), 51 (30).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, microwave irradiation, alternative preparation shown,
Bucherer-Bergs Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-promoted facile and rapid synthesis procedure for the efficient
synthesis of 5,5-disubstituted hydantoins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Safari, Javad; Gandomi-Ravandi, Soheila; Javadian, Leila
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2013), 43(23), 3115-3120

