$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Alkenyl Spirohydantoins 2a-c; General
Procedure To a 100 mL round-bottom flask equipped with a reflux condenser
containing 50% aq EtOH (30 mL) were added the appropriate unsaturated
ketone 1 (5 mmol), NaCN (0.490 g, 10 mmol), and (NH4)2CO3 (1.920 g, 20
mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred and heated to reflux for 24 h.
The mixture was then cooled to r.t. and filtered. The pH of the filtrate
was adjusted to ~2 by carefully adding of concd HCl. The filtrate was
placed in a refrigerator for better crystallization of the products. The
products were separated by filtration and dried in a vacuum oven (45
°C/20 mbar, 24 h). Purity of the products was checked by TLC.
cis-6-Allyl-1,3-diazaspiro[4.4]nonane-2,4-dione (2a)
cis-6-(2-Methylallyl)-1,3-diazaspiro[4.5]decane-2,4-dione (2c) Yield:
0.856 g (77%); crystalline solid. mp 208 °C; Rf = 0.55
(toluene-EtOAc-MeOH, 5:5:1). IR (KBr): 3289, 2926, 1767, 1714, 1406 cm-1.
1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.75-1.05 (m, 1 H), 1.17-1.49 (m, 2 H), 1.67
(s, 3 H), 1.72-2.1 (m, 8 H), 4.67-4.75 (m, 2 H), 6.85 (br s, 1 H), 8.47
(br s, 1 H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 21.8, 21.9, 25.0, 27.3, 35.2,
38.8, 39.3, 67.3, 113.1, 142.2, 157.1, 177.2. Anal. Calcd for
C12H18N2O2·H2O: C, 59.98; H, 8.39; N, 11.66. Found: C, 60.15; H, 8.42; N,
11.77.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Bucherer-Strecker reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
